      "message": "Quick preliminary question: is it an issue if Encrypted AD types are decrypted using different keys in the storage? Currently you attempt to decrypt all ED using a unique key.\n\nThe file architecture could still be improved with the following changes:\n\n1. Reduce the helper function DecryptEncryptedData() to _just_ perform the decryption for one AD Encrypted Data element, with one key:\n```\n// Attempt to decrypt one Encrypted Data AD type, using the provided\n// key material. Appends the decrypted data to the output buffer.\nbool Decrypt(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e const\u0026 data,\n             std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e const\u0026 key,\n             std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e const\u0026 iv,\n             std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u0026 output);\n``` \n\n2. I don\u0027t see it as necessary to keep the separate helper GetEncAdvFieldsInfo()\nExtractEncryptedData() should do the following:\n\n```\n// 1. extract key material from storage bin to the following variable.\n// This could be performed in an helper function `ExtractKeyMaterial()`\nstd::vector\u003cstd::pair\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u003e\u003e keys_and_ivs;\n\nbool decrypt_failure \u003d false;\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e decrypted_data;\n\n// 2. iterate over GAP data\nfor (..) {\n    ad_type \u003d ..;\n    data \u003d ..;\n    \n    if (ad_type \u003d\u003d AD_TYPE_ENCRYPTED_DATA) {\n       bool decrypted \u003d false;\n       for (auto const\u0026 [key, iv] : keys_and_ivs) {\n           if ((decrypted \u003d Decrypt(data, key, iv, decrypted_data)) {\n               break;\n           }\n       }\n       decrypt_failure |\u003d !decrypted;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nDepending on whether you intend to decrypt the data in place, or to a different buffer, you may adapt the logic to change where the decrypted data is produced.",
